## Orchestration
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
- Codex is the primary orchestrator. It selects workers, owns the plan, resolves
  conflicts, applies the final verification gate, reconciles the result, and is
  the only agent that reports completion to Dillon.
- Hermes is a subordinate local execution and background-runtime layer. Claude,
  Grok, Cursor, and other models are bounded specialist workers or tools. They
  return evidence to Codex and never become parallel command centers.
- Marketing Chief is the Codex orchestration role and the only canonical queue
  writer.
- Use the smallest useful specialist set. Never exceed three concurrent workers.
- Standard marketing flow: Research -> Strategy/AEO -> Content/Copy -> Visual
  Direction/Build -> Independent Critic/QA -> gated Delivery.
- Every handoff must include workflow and step IDs, task, constraints, source
  locators, upstream artifacts, token budget, timeout, acceptance checks,
  evidence paths, risks, and approval state.
- Workers return bounded artifacts and evidence. They do not edit generated vault
  files, canonical queue state, approvals, or durable client decisions.
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
## Verification and delivery
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
- A completion claim needs tests, logs, screenshots, source citations, or another
  reviewable artifact. Agent confidence is not evidence.
- UI work must be checked at desktop and mobile widths. Verify rendering, CTA
  visibility, keyboard access, reduced motion, overflow, and the browser console.
- Visual work must use verified client assets and compare the output with the
  approved reference or prior accepted version.
- The critic must score brand match, clarity, conversion intent, factual support,
  accessibility, and technical integrity. The default pass threshold is 8/10,
  with no critical category below 7.
- Sending, scheduling, publishing, spend, account changes, destructive actions,
  and new public destinations remain gated by the canonical policy and exact
  current authority.
System.Management.Automation.RemoteException
